---
import InfoLayout from "@/layouts/InfoLayout.astro";

export const prerender = true;
---

<InfoLayout
  heading="Support"
  description="Get help with Quick Pantry, recipe imports, account access, and AI client connections."
>
  <p>
    Report a problem or ask a question through
    <a href="https://github.com/jamesqquick/pantry-plan/issues">Quick Pantry's GitHub issues</a>.
    Include what you were trying to do, what happened, and the error message
    if one appeared. The issue tracker is public, so leave out passwords,
    tokens, and private recipes or account details.
  </p>

  <section aria-labelledby="account-help">
    <h2 id="account-help">Account access</h2>
    <p>
      <a href="/login">Sign in</a> with email/password or Google. For a forgotten
      password, use <a href="/forgot-password">Forgot password</a> to request a
      reset link. You can manage your name, password, and Google connection in
      <a href="/profile">Profile</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="import-help">
    <h2 id="import-help">Imports and connectivity</h2>
    <p>
      Review imported recipe drafts before saving. Some recipe URLs cannot be
      parsed, and photo import is available only when enabled for your account.
      If the app shows an offline message, reconnect to load live data or make
      changes.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="connection-help">
    <h2 id="connection-help">ChatGPT and other AI clients</h2>
    <p>
      The hosted MCP endpoint is <a href="https://quickpantry.app/mcp">https://quickpantry.app/mcp</a>.
      The ChatGPT plugin uses your own OAuth grant. Other MCP clients can use
      a key created in Profile. Revoke OAuth connections or MCP keys in
      <a href="/profile">Profile</a> when you want to stop their access.
    </p>
    <p>
      ChatGPT's recipe and meal-planning tools return normal chat responses.
      They do not manage grocery orders, make purchases, or delete recipes.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="data-help">
    <h2 id="data-help">Privacy and data questions</h2>
    <p>
      Read <a href="/privacy">Privacy</a> and <a href="/terms">Terms of use</a>.
      For a privacy or data request, open a GitHub issue with a general
      description of the request, without posting private account information.
    </p>
  </section>
</InfoLayout>
